From: Mate Molnar <matemolnar88@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pvr: pass a valid macrotile array address on simple parameter format v1

The macrotile array size is 0 on these cores and Mesa then passes
PVR_DEV_ADDR_INVALID for PM_MTILE_ARRAY / ISP_MTILE_BASE. The vendor DDK 1.9
always programs a valid address (a 16-byte pad in front of its MList). Give
the hardware a small valid buffer. (Scaling the region header count by 4
instead was wrong: the TE overran the region header buffer and the
geometry job faulted at the USC code heap base.)
---
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_job_render.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_job_render.c
@@ -414,7 +414,9 @@
    VkResult result;
 
    /* Valid case - see rogue_get_macrotile_array_size() */
-   if (mta_size == 0) {
+   if (mta_size == 0 &&
+       PVR_GET_FEATURE_VALUE(dev_info, simple_parameter_format_version, 0) !=
+          1) {
       rt_dataset->mta_bo = NULL;
 
       for (uint32_t i = 0; i < num_rt_datas; i++)
@@ -423,9 +425,14 @@
       return VK_SUCCESS;
    }
 
+   /* Simple parameter format v1 has no macrotile array either, but the vendor
+    * driver still programs a valid PM_MTILE_ARRAY / ISP_MTILE_BASE address (a
+    * 16-byte pad at the head of its MList allocation). Give the hardware a
+    * small valid buffer instead of PVR_DEV_ADDR_INVALID.
+    */
    result = pvr_bo_alloc(device,
                          device->heaps.general_heap,
-                         mta_size * num_rt_datas,
+                         mta_size ? mta_size * num_rt_datas : 64U,
                          ROGUE_CR_PM_MTILE_ARRAY_BASE_ADDR_ALIGNMENT,
                          PVR_BO_ALLOC_FLAG_GPU_UNCACHED,
                          &rt_dataset->mta_bo);
